WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.816
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.816 --> 00:00:05.100
which takes about forty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.798
You'll name the three places sequel
server can depend on certificates that

4
00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:14.163
A D C S issued, and the issuer that P
K I and Certificates assigns to each.

5
00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:17.774
You'll explain why an expiring T
L S certificate breaks clients,

6
00:00:17.774 --> 00:00:21.387
while an expiring signing
certificate doesn't lock anyone out.

7
00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:25.227
You'll run the kit's certificate
dependency list over fixtures

8
00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:28.624
and read its class, issuer,
expiry and action for each row.

9
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:30.950
And you'll say why certificate-mapped,

10
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.725
type C, logins aren't
migrated to Entra logins.

11
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:36.287
Before you start, finish Module 7.

12
00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:40.782
And remember from Module 6: an
endpoint that authenticates

13
00:00:40.782 --> 00:00:44.176
with NTLM or negotiate
is also an NTLM source.

14
00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:49.630
The lab runs in PowerShell 7, in the kit
you unzipped into the F M W Labs folder.
